course: dictionary
lesson: 12530
title: Despised
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Despised means hated and looked down on by others. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «The villain was despised by everyone in the village, and nobody would help him.» The clue is nobody would help him: people did not like him at all, so despised means hated.
explain: Despise is the verb, and despised is its past form. To despise someone is to dislike them very strongly and think they are worthless. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The villain was hated and looked down on by everyone» still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Despised is stronger than disliked. «The weasels were despised by the river animals» tells you the animals looked down on the weasels, not just that they were a bit annoying. Strong feeling is part of the meaning.
fact: Despised means hated and looked down on by others.
fact: To despise someone is to dislike them very strongly and think they are worthless.
fact: The phrase «despised and rejected» comes from the Bible, in the book of Isaiah, and Christians believe it describes Jesus.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the weasels and stoats are despised by the river animals, and Toad is despised by the bargewoman.
fact: In history, some groups were wrongly despised because of who they were.
exercise: «The cruel king was despised by his people.» What does despised mean? | Tired out after a long day | Forgotten by everyone | *Hated and looked down on | Loved and praised
exercise: Which word means almost the same as despise? | Admire | *Scorn | Forgive | Greet
exercise: «Toad was despised by the bargewoman, so she never gave him a kind word.» What does despised show? | She wanted to be his friend | She had lost her boat | She was afraid of him for a moment | *She disliked him very strongly and looked down on him
test: Which is the main difference between disliked and despised? | Despised means happy and friendly | *Despised is much stronger: it means hated and looked down on | They mean exactly the same thing | Disliked is stronger than despised
test: «Some groups in history were wrongly despised because of who they were.» What does wrongly suggest? | They were forgotten after a while | They deserved to be hated for what they did | *It was unfair, because they did not deserve to be hated | Everyone liked them very much
exam: Which sentence uses despised correctly? | The sunny morning despised the dog and made it sleepy | *The bully was despised by the whole class for being cruel | Dad despised the warm bread at breakfast, so he ate two slices | We despised the new park and happily played there all day
